IMPORT prelude

-- Motor Vehicles (Third-Party Risks and Compensation) Act 1960 (Singapore),
-- 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 January 2026.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/MVTPRCA1960.txt
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Written straight from the text with the writing-l4-rules
-- skill and nothing else: no pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test
-- pass, no human gate. Observations, not checked findings.
--
-- SCOPE. ss 2, 3, 4 and 9 -- the compulsory-insurance offence and its defence,
-- what makes a policy comply, and the insurer's duty to satisfy a judgment
-- against its insured. s 9 is the heart of the Act: it is what makes the
-- insurance worth anything to the injured third party, and it is where every
-- deadline lives.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: ss 5-8 (settlement agreements and composite settlements),
-- ss 10-24 (insolvency, information duties, surrender of certificates,
-- deposits, the Public Trustee's powers, penalties, rules). The Schedule of
-- specified territories is a fact supplied.

§ `Motor Vehicles (Third-Party Risks and Compensation) Act 1960`

§§ `2 -- Interpretation`

-- s 2: "'relevant amount' means $5,000 or, where another amount has been
-- prescribed under section 20 by the appropriate Minister ..., the prescribed
-- amount".
--
-- Carried as a fact rather than the literal 5000, because the whole point of
-- the definition is that the Minister may change it and the Act then reads
-- differently. An encoding that hard-coded 5000 would be wrong the day an
-- order is gazetted.
DECLARE Prescribed HAS
    `the relevant amount in dollars`  IS A NUMBER

-- s 2 "specified person", paragraph (b), which is the limb section 9 uses:
-- a person entitled to the benefit of a s 9(1)(b) judgment who, AT THE TIME THE
-- JUDGMENT IS GIVEN, falls within one of five descriptions. The timing matters
-- and is part of each fact's name.
DECLARE Claimant HAS
    `name`                                          IS A STRING
    `below 21 years of age when the judgment was given`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(i)
    `lacks capacity within the Mental Capacity Act 2008 section 4 when the judgment was given` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(ii)
    `unrepresented when the judgment was given`     IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(iii)
    `isolated under the Infectious Diseases Act 1976 section 15 when the judgment was given` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(iv)
    `in legal custody in a place of detention when the judgment was given` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(v)

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant is a specified person for section 9` IF
        `the claimant`'s `below 21 years of age when the judgment was given`
    OR  `the claimant`'s `lacks capacity within the Mental Capacity Act 2008 section 4 when the judgment was given`
    OR  `the claimant`'s `unrepresented when the judgment was given`
    OR  `the claimant`'s `isolated under the Infectious Diseases Act 1976 section 15 when the judgment was given`
    OR  `the claimant`'s `in legal custody in a place of detention when the judgment was given`

§§ `4 -- Requirements in respect of policies`

-- s 4(1): "In order to comply with the requirements of this Act, a policy of
-- insurance must, subject to subsection (4), be a policy which --
--   (a) is issued by an insurer who at the time the policy is issued is
--       lawfully carrying on motor insurance business in Singapore; and
--   (b) insures the person, persons or classes of persons that may be specified
--       in the policy in respect of any liability which may be incurred by him,
--       her or them in respect of the death of or bodily injury to any person
--       caused by or arising out of the use of the motor vehicle in Singapore
--       and in any territory specified in the Schedule."
DECLARE Policy HAS
    `in force in relation to this use`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4(1)(a)
    `the insurer was lawfully carrying on motor insurance business in Singapore when issued` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4(1)(b)
    `insures the user against liability for death or bodily injury arising out of the use of the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4(9): the certificate, which s 9(1) makes the gateway to the whole of
    -- the insurer's duty.
    `a certificate of insurance has been issued under section 4(9)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the policy` IS A Policy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the policy complies with the requirements of this Act` IF
        `the policy`'s `the insurer was lawfully carrying on motor insurance business in Singapore when issued`
    AND `the policy`'s `insures the user against liability for death or bodily injury arising out of the use of the vehicle`

-- s 4(4): "A policy of insurance is not, by virtue of subsection (1)(b),
-- required to cover --
--   (a) liability in respect of --
--        (i)  the death of or bodily injury sustained by a person (A) who is in
--             the employment of a person insured by the policy, where the death
--             or bodily injury arises out of and in the course of A's
--             employment; or
--        (ii) the death of or bodily injury sustained by a platform worker (B)
--             who provides a platform service for a platform operator insured
--             by the policy, where ... in the course of B's provision of the
--             platform service for that platform operator; or
--   (b) any contractual liability."
--
-- Both employment limbs are two-part: the status AND that the injury arose out
-- of and in the course of it. Status alone does not take the liability outside
-- the cover.
DECLARE Liability HAS
    `for death or bodily injury caused by or arising out of the use of the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injured person is in the employment of a person insured by the policy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injury arose out of and in the course of that employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injured person is a platform worker providing a platform service for a platform operator insured by the policy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injury arose out of and in the course of providing that platform service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a contractual liability`  IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the liability` IS A Liability
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4(4)(a)(i) takes the liability outside the required cover` IF
        `the liability`'s `the injured person is in the employment of a person insured by the policy`
    AND `the liability`'s `the injury arose out of and in the course of that employment`

GIVEN `the liability` IS A Liability
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4(4)(a)(ii) takes the liability outside the required cover` IF
        `the liability`'s `the injured person is a platform worker providing a platform service for a platform operator insured by the policy`
    AND `the liability`'s `the injury arose out of and in the course of providing that platform service`

GIVEN `the liability` IS A Liability
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the liability is one a policy need not cover` IF
        `section 4(4)(a)(i) takes the liability outside the required cover` `the liability`
    OR  `section 4(4)(a)(ii) takes the liability outside the required cover` `the liability`
    OR  `the liability`'s `it is a contractual liability`

-- The liability s 4(1)(b) actually requires to be covered, which is the phrase
-- s 9(1) picks up.
GIVEN `the liability` IS A Liability
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the liability is required to be covered by section 4(1)(b)` IF
        `the liability`'s `for death or bodily injury caused by or arising out of the use of the vehicle`
    AND NOT `the liability is one a policy need not cover` `the liability`

§§ `3 -- Users of motor vehicles to be insured against third-party risks`

-- s 3(1): "it is not lawful for any person to use or to cause or permit any
-- other person to use -- (a) a motor vehicle in Singapore; or (b) a motor
-- vehicle which is registered in Singapore in any territory specified in the
-- Schedule, unless there is in force in relation to the use of the motor
-- vehicle by that person ... a policy of insurance or a security in respect of
-- third-party risks that complies with the requirements of this Act."
DECLARE Use HAS
    `the user`                      IS A STRING
    `the vehicle is used in Singapore`  IS A BOOLEAN           -- s 3(1)(a)
    `the vehicle is registered in Singapore and used in a territory specified in the Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3(1)(b)
    `the policy`                    IS A Policy
    -- s 3(1) offers a security as the alternative to a policy; s 21 applies the
    -- Act to securities. Whether a complying security is in force is a fact.
    `a complying security is in force in respect of third-party risks` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3(1) applies to the use` IF
        `the use`'s `the vehicle is used in Singapore`
    OR  `the use`'s `the vehicle is registered in Singapore and used in a territory specified in the Schedule`

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cover is in force for the use` IF
        `a complying policy is in force`  `the use`
    OR  `the use`'s `a complying security is in force in respect of third-party risks`

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a complying policy is in force` IF
        `the use`'s `the policy`'s `in force in relation to this use`
    AND `the policy complies with the requirements of this Act` (`the use`'s `the policy`)

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use contravenes section 3(1)` IF
        `section 3(1) applies to the use` `the use`
    AND NOT `cover is in force for the use` `the use`

-- s 3(4): "A person shall not be guilty of an offence under this section if the
-- person proves -- (a) that the motor vehicle did not belong to the person and
-- was not in the person's possession under a contract of hiring or loan;
-- (b) that the person was using the vehicle in the course of the person's
-- employment; and (c) that the person neither knew nor had reason to believe
-- that there was not in force ... a policy of insurance or such security as
-- complies with the provisions of this Act."
--
-- Three limbs joined by "and": the employee driver's defence, and the burden is
-- on the accused ("if the person proves"). Whether it was discharged is a fact.
DECLARE Section3Defence HAS
    `the vehicle did not belong to the person and was not in the person's possession under a contract of hiring or loan` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `the person was using the vehicle in the course of the person's employment` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `the person neither knew nor had reason to believe that no complying cover was in force` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)

GIVEN `the defence` IS A Section3Defence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 3(4) defence is made out` IF
        `the defence`'s `the vehicle did not belong to the person and was not in the person's possession under a contract of hiring or loan`
    AND `the defence`'s `the person was using the vehicle in the course of the person's employment`
    AND `the defence`'s `the person neither knew nor had reason to believe that no complying cover was in force`

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use, `the defence` IS A Section3Defence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty of an offence under section 3` IF
        `the use contravenes section 3(1)` `the use`
    AND NOT `the section 3(4) defence is made out` `the defence`

-- s 3(3): disqualification from holding or obtaining a driving licence for
-- 12 months, "unless the court for special reasons thinks fit to order
-- otherwise". A mandatory consequence with a judicial escape, so the escape is
-- a fact and the rule says what follows without it.
GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
    , `the defence` IS A Section3Defence
    , `the court found special reasons to order otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is to be disqualified for 12 months under section 3(3)` IF
        `the person is guilty of an offence under section 3` `the use` `the defence`
    AND NOT `the court found special reasons to order otherwise`

§§ `9 -- Duty of insurers to satisfy judgments against persons insured`

-- s 9(1): the gateway. "if after a certificate of insurance has been issued
-- under section 4(9) ..., judgment in respect of any liability required to be
-- covered by a policy under section 4(1)(b) (being a liability covered by the
-- terms of the policy) is obtained against any person insured by the policy,
-- then, EVEN THOUGH the insurer may be entitled to avoid or cancel or may have
-- avoided or cancelled the policy, the following apply to the insurer".
--
-- The "even though" is the whole purpose of the section: the third party's
-- claim survives the insurer's rights against its own insured.
DECLARE Judgment HAS
    `the claimant`                  IS A Claimant
    `the policy`                    IS A Policy
    `the liability`                 IS A Liability
    `the liability is covered by the terms of the policy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `obtained against a person insured by the policy` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9(1)(a)-(b): the sum payable EXCLUDING costs and judgment interest.
    `the sum payable excluding costs and interest in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    -- s 9(1)(b)(i): payment to the Public Trustee happens only where the
    -- judgment so requires AND the claimant is a specified person.
    `the judgment requires the sum to be paid to the Public Trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9(6)(a)
    `the insurer had notice of the bringing of the proceedings before or within 7 days after they commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9(6)(b)
    `enforcement on the judgment is stayed pending an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9(6)(c): cancellation before the event, plus one of three dealings with
    -- the certificate.
    `the policy was cancelled by mutual consent or under the policy before the event` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate was surrendered or a statutory declaration of loss made before the event` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)(i)
    `the certificate was surrendered or such a declaration made within 14 days after the cancellation took effect` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)(ii)
    `the insurer commenced proceedings for failure to surrender the certificate within the 14 day period` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)(iii)
    -- s 9(7)
    `the insurer obtained a declaration of entitlement to avoid for non-disclosure or misrepresentation in an action commenced before or within 3 months after the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9(1) is engaged` IF
        `the judgment`'s `the policy`'s `a certificate of insurance has been issued under section 4(9)`
    AND `the liability is required to be covered by section 4(1)(b)` (`the judgment`'s `the liability`)
    AND `the judgment`'s `the liability is covered by the terms of the policy`
    AND `the judgment`'s `obtained against a person insured by the policy`

-- s 9(6)(c): the three certificate limbs are joined by "or", and all of them
-- sit under the requirement that the policy was cancelled before the event.
GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 9(6)(c) certificate dealing occurred` IF
        `the judgment`'s `the certificate was surrendered or a statutory declaration of loss made before the event`
    OR  `the judgment`'s `the certificate was surrendered or such a declaration made within 14 days after the cancellation took effect`
    OR  `the judgment`'s `the insurer commenced proceedings for failure to surrender the certificate within the 14 day period`

GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9(6)(c) bars payment` IF
        `the judgment`'s `the policy was cancelled by mutual consent or under the policy before the event`
    AND `a section 9(6)(c) certificate dealing occurred` `the judgment`

-- s 9(6)(a)-(c) and s 9(7): four separate bars, any of which stops payment.
-- (a) is expressed as a condition ("unless ... the insurer had notice"), so the
-- bar is the ABSENCE of notice.
GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no sum is payable by the insurer` IF
        `section 9(6)(a) bars payment` `the judgment`
    ..  `the judgment`'s `enforcement on the judgment is stayed pending an appeal`
    ..  `section 9(6)(c) bars payment` `the judgment`
    OR  `the judgment`'s `the insurer obtained a declaration of entitlement to avoid for non-disclosure or misrepresentation in an action commenced before or within 3 months after the proceedings`

GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9(6)(a) bars payment` IF
    NOT `the judgment`'s `the insurer had notice of the bringing of the proceedings before or within 7 days after they commenced`

-- s 9(1)(a) and (b): the relevant amount splits a PERMISSION from a DUTY.
--   (a) at or below the relevant amount -- the insurer MAY pay the claimant;
--   (b) above it -- the insurer MUST pay, and to the Public Trustee where the
--       claimant is a specified person and the judgment so requires.
--
-- "does not exceed" in (a) and "exceeds" in (b) partition the range at the
-- relevant amount itself, which falls in (a).
GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment, `the prescribed` IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sum exceeds the relevant amount` IF
    `the judgment`'s `the sum payable excluding costs and interest in dollars`
        GREATER THAN `the prescribed`'s `the relevant amount in dollars`

GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment, `the prescribed` IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the insurer may pay the claimant under section 9(1)(a)` IF
        `section 9(1) is engaged` `the judgment`
    AND NOT `no sum is payable by the insurer` `the judgment`
    AND NOT `the sum exceeds the relevant amount` `the judgment` `the prescribed`

GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment, `the prescribed` IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the insurer must pay under section 9(1)(b)` IF
        `section 9(1) is engaged` `the judgment`
    AND NOT `no sum is payable by the insurer` `the judgment`
    AND `the sum exceeds the relevant amount` `the judgment` `the prescribed`

-- s 9(1)(b)(i): to the Public Trustee as trustee for the claimant, where the
-- claimant is a specified person AND the judgment requires it; (ii) otherwise
-- to the claimant.
GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment, `the prescribed` IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `payment must be made to the Public Trustee` IF
        `the insurer must pay under section 9(1)(b)` `the judgment` `the prescribed`
    AND `the claimant is a specified person for section 9` (`the judgment`'s `the claimant`)
    AND `the judgment`'s `the judgment requires the sum to be paid to the Public Trustee`

GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment, `the prescribed` IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `payment must be made to the claimant under section 9(1)(b)(ii)` IF
        `the insurer must pay under section 9(1)(b)` `the judgment` `the prescribed`
    AND NOT `payment must be made to the Public Trustee` `the judgment` `the prescribed`
